WEBVTT

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.070
Go! Shock!! Gourmet!! Gourmet!!

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.840
Go! Shock!!

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.180
Friends who can eat the same dream

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.020
Friends who share the same future

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.720
With you guys

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.720
It’s first-rate gourmet my way!

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.390
If we join forces

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.360
We’ll be invincible

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.700
Come on, let’s show ‘em

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.870
Delicious food gives life

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:09.010
So be thankful for everything and

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.080
Let’s eat!!

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.020
We can’t lose!! We can’t be stopped!!

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.150
We ain’t gonna let ‘em have that

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.320
We’re gonna win it!! Shock! 
Shock! Gourmet king!!

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.330
Spiked Punch!! Infinity!!

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.030
I’ll punch through with this fist

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:33.070
First-rate gourmet my way!

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.940
Let’s gather ‘round the table

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.940
For the sake of tomorrow

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.140
Let’s go! Go! Gourmet!!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.850
Someone once said...

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.720
There's a jaguar that 
drips with rich butter...

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.790
Buttered Potato Jaguar!

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.930
Buttered Potato Jaguar
Mattsu-san from Osaka Prefecture's creation!

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:04.070
There are peaches that are as 
smooth as mozzarella cheese...

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:09.270
Mozzarella Peacheese!

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.900
Mozzarella Peacheese
The Milk Pudding-san from Gifu Prefecture's creation!

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.440
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.680
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.650
There are two training ingredients 
left on the list the IGO President,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:24.480
Ichiryu, made for Toriko.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.120
One of them is somewhere in the Lost Forest,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.220
the Human World's vastest sea of trees.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.160
Fortune-telling Sushi
Monchy

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.560
Toriko decided to have Monchy, the 
fortune-telling sushi crafstman,

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.690
Sushi

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.100
divine the ingredient's exact location.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.830
Then, the Four Kings Gourmet Hunters, 
along with Komatsu and a few others,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.300
captured the Madam Fish to be used 
as an ingredient in the Fortune Roll.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:51.680
Toriko Faints in Agony?! Capture 
the World's Stinkiest Ingredient!

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.020
That's one big shark!

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.850
It's a Woozy Shark.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.960
Nothin' to worry about!

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.790
The shark's just drunk!

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.300
This is white wine!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.970
I thought I smelled the 
scent of wine out here!

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.240
That's the Spirits Sea for you!

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.580
Delicious!

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.380
Um, Spirits Sea?

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.950
This part of the ocean is made 
of various kinds of booze,

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:33.120
like wine, whiskey, beer, and shochu.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.920
Toriko, you can see it now!

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.760
Spirits Archipelago!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.890
Spirits... You mean "spirits" 
as in strong alcohol?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.330
Yeah.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.100
Champagne Island, Cocktail Isle...

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.170
A collection of islands where you 
can get various kinds of booze.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.600
If you're under 20, though, 
this area is forbidden.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.070
Komatsu, you're okay age-wise, right?

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.910
Of course!

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.580
I mean, I'm the same age as you, Toriko-san!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.710
You're the same age as me?!

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:03.480
Uh-huh!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.520
We're almost there!

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.050
This island kind of looks like a wine glass.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.690
A paradise of booze, Firewater Island!

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.260
Thank you!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.860
Um, why did we come to this island?

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.470
Well, when I went back to see Monchy...

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.940
Dumbass! You think I can make the 
Fortune Roll with Madam Fish alone?!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.710
You <i>can't</i>?!

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.510
What about the vinegared rice?!

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:35.280
Without vinegar for the vinegared 
rice, I can't make the Fortune Roll!

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.110
So would you just get 
me some vinegar, moron?!

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.680
And so here we are...

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.350
Then we've come to this 
island to get vinegar?

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.550
That's the idea.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.790
We need to ferment the finest 
alcohol on Firewater Island

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.930
to make the so-called king of 
all vinegars, King Vinegar.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.460
King Vinegar! That's ultrahigh grade vinegar!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.770
So rare that it hardly ever hits the market!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.570
That oughta make for some 
yummy vinegared rice, right?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.610
Yep! Wow, I can't wait!

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.180
A charging drunken bull!

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.710
A Drunken Cow!

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:13.280
Drunken Cow (Mammalian 
Beast) Capture Level 30

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.720
This cow is on Chief 
Mansom's Full Course Menu!

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.250
I didn't think it'd be on this island, too!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.790
Knife!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.730
And now we've got a nice 
snack to go with the booze.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:33.000
Why was there a rampaging bull here?!

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.140
This is no kind of paradise!

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.740
All the Beasts on this island are drunk.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.240
And apparently, some of 
them are violent drunks.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.610
They're all drunk?!

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.650
This smell...

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.680
A well of high-grade brandy!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.150
A mellow aroma...

00:05:55.150 --> 00:06:00.390
This deep amber color is like a jewel!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.130
There's another one!

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.270
A Brandy Tiger!

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:10.440
Brandy Tiger (Mammalian 
Beast) Capture Level 53

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.400
A tiger with top shelf brandy for blood...

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.670
But don't worry. As long 
as you don't drink it...

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.740
I mean, as long as you don't bother it 
when it's drinking, it won't attack you.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.150
Even though it's drunk, I'm glad 
it's a mild-mannered tiger.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.410
Well, since we're here...

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.250
Let's drink!

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.690
Delicious!

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.990
It's got a dry, mature flavor!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.900
I think it'd go good with 
that Drunken Cow from before!

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.530
Have a sip, Komatsu.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:42.400
It's 80-proof, which is perfect!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.040
I'm not really one to drink...

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.140
It'll be fine! Look!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.370
There's some Turmeric Turds.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:52.140
If you chow down on that, you won't get 
drunk, no matter how much you guzzle.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.810
That's turmeric?! Turds?! Which one?!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.420
Turmeric Turds!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.850
Anyway, eat it!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.120
With this island's booze, 
never mind a hangover,

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.190
I hear there are some people who stay 
drunk forever and can't go home again!

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.490
Drunk forever?!

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:11.760
Well, I feel like I could drink up 
all the booze on Firewater Island!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.660
Right, Toriko-san!

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.100
But is that what we came here for?

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.100
A beer waterfall!

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.410
The sparkling carbonation is so beautiful!

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.240
And there are Chip Trees, too!

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:30.050
The bark of the trees are potato chips!

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.280
Crispy and superb salt seasoning!

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.720
It goes great with the bitter beer!

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.220
Natural Aluminum Cabbage!

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.660
There's Onion Cheese, too!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.630
This'll be another great drinking snack!

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.760
And there's a butterfly made of potato chips!

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.230
It's a Salted Seaweed Butterfly! 
It looks delicious!

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.070
Rain?

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.240
This is...

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.740
...not your everyday rain!

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.880
It's raining champagne!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.920
The fizziness feels so good!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.580
And it's delicious!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.120
Yummy rain!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.520
What the hell? Was it just 
a passing champagne shower?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.430
It's cloudy again!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.060
Now what?!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.500
Tequila rain? Vodka rain?

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.230
It's not a cloud!

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.370
E-Emerald Dragon!

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.270
Fine wine gushes out of its back...

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.340
That legendary dragon?!

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:34.680
Emerald Dragon (Insect 
Beast) Capture Level 78

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.680
Yeah. We're in deep Turmeric Turd.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.680
This guy ain't only tough, 
he's got a short temper.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.650
I don't know if I can take 'im 
down, plastered like this!

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:46.750
Huh? He's not attacking...

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.290
This is...

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.220
Knocking?!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.930
What's all the hubbub?!

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.070
That's...

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.100
...Knocking Master Jiro!

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.840
It was you two!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:11.010
Interested in takin' an Emerald Wine bath?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.110
Awesome!

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.080
It really is an emerald-colored bath!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.250
One bottle of this wine costs five 
million, if you can believe it,

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.150
and I'm takin' a bath in it.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:23.360
Thank you for the bath! {instead of the usual "Thank you for the food", though they use the same expression as always here}

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.430
What a waste!

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.770
You shouldn't waste even one drop of booze.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.770
That reminds me of Grinpatch 
from the Gourmet Corp.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:42.870
Delicious.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.810
The alcohol here is delicious,

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:48.210
but don't drink at home, kids!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.020
Who are you talkin' to?

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.620
I never expected to meet you here, Jiro-san!

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.520
Do you often come to this island?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.890
Sometimes even eight days a week, I'd say.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.660
More than every day?!

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:04.230
I see...

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.670
It seems you two are making smooth progress.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.540
Thank you!

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.340
Jiro, it's thanks to you.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.410
In the Gourmet World,

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:20.680
you taught me what my weakness was.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:25.480
So ever since then, I've been 
workin' hard doing my training,

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:28.250
makin' myself fit for the Gourmet World.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.790
Although it seems the crucial Gourmet 
World that you aspire to get to

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.690
is becoming a turbulent place these days.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.700
Good grief...

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.230
Those two...

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:45.170
I may end up having to go there myself...

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:50.070
Ah, well... I'll cross that 
bridge when I come to it.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:55.710
Drink!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.680
It's my treat!

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.080
Thank you!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.520
Sake tastes good in all ages.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.520
Delicious!

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.760
On rainy days, on nice days,

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.960
sake is always delicious.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.430
What changes is the hearts 
of those who drink it.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.890
Another one!

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:13.430
Let's keep drinking!

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:17.530
And my heart changes the flavor of the sake.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:22.370
I wish I could spend the rest of my 
life calmly drinking delicious sake...

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.870
Jiro-san!

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:30.780
Sake

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:28.180
What kind of alcohol is this?

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.910
It's my Full Course Drink.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.380
Then...?!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.920
D-D-Doham Spring Sake?!

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:40.590
Uh... That surprised me so 
much, I'm totally sober now.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:41.490
You wanna drink it?

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:42.690
I totally wanna drink it!

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.060
I don't believe it...

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.660
I get to drink precious sake that can 
only be found in the Gourmet World?!

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.400
Sorry.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.100
Sake

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.100
I drank it all.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.540
Oh, well...

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:59.270
Soon, you guys will be able to get 
your own in the Gourmet World.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.710
There's still plenty of booze on this island,

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:06.050
from Cocktail Lake to Refined Sake Pond.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.510
So drink up!

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.320
Right!

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.320
Yeah!

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:11.950
Huh? I feel like we're forgetting 
something important...

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.960
Idiots! Idiots!

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.500
Fortune-telling Sushi
Monchy

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.500
Not bad!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.640
So you brought me some King Vinegar, dummy?

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:43.950
King Vinegar

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:33.970
I drank so much, never mind 
a hangover the next day.

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:36.940
It lasted a whole week!

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.750
I prepared the vinegar, just like you said.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.950
Even though we forgot our goal at first 
and drank straight for two days...

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:47.090
Monchy, make that Fortune Roll!

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.590
Idiot!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.290
That's echoing through my head!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.090
You think I can make it with the 
Madam Fish and King Vinegar alone?!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:57.400
That's not nearly enough fillings!

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.200
Do not treat the Fortune Roll lightly!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.440
W-What should we do, Toriko-san?

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.840
Ask <i>him</i>, I guess...

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.410
A Fortune Roll, huh?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:13.280
I figured a Reviver like you would 
know a good ingredient for it.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.550
Plus there's the pompadour 
connection you have with Jiro...

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:18.380
What kind of connection is that?!

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.920
Come on, Teppei, you gotta 
have somethin' for me...

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.720
Well, let me see...

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:26.960
Recently, I revived Café Ants,

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.430
which have torsos made of coffee beans, 
heads of milk, behinds of syrup,

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:33.100
and if you pour hot water on 
them, they make excellent coffee.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:36.870
And Salmon Roe Grapes, which 
went extinct 40 years ago.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.840
Finally, what I discovered in geologic 
stratum thousands of years old,

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:43.110
Mochi Rocks, which are, of 
course, mochi-like rocks.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.780
I don't think any of 'em would 
be good for the Fortune Roll...

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.680
That's it. Sorry.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.750
But it's still impressive!

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.350
I've never seen any of 
those ingredients before.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.290
Viva, Revivers!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.390
Yeah, but even among Revivers these days,

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.790
there are those who go about 
reviving things willy-nilly.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:05.530
Hazardous ingredients that are 
prohibited from the market

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.130
and quarantined organisms that 
are dangerous if let free...

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.500
They revive without permission from the IGO.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.040
There's no end to the rule-breaking 
of these Revivers.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:16.640
Well...

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.210
I'm speaking mostly of myself...

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.810
You?!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:22.780
Recently, I revived something incredible

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.510
and now I'm in a real fix.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.280
What's the ingredient?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.990
The stinkiest ingredient in the world!

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.390
The Durian Bomb.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:34.990
Durian Bomb...

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:37.890
A tree fruit that's also 
called the Smell Bomb.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:42.560
Apparently, a long time ago 
it was used as a weapon.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.070
I hear the IGO restricted its circulation.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.740
And a fruit like that is a 
good fit for the Fortune Roll?

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.110
For making an impact, it's perfect.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:57.180
In just a moment, the train will 
be arriving at Durian Station.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.310
Close the windows!

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.820
W-What's going on?!

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.750
Get ready to go, Komatsu.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.930
Stinks!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:20.070
Durian

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.860
The train escaped! And nobody else is here!

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.400
It's an unmanned station.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.100
It smells so bad here that hardly 
any passengers ever get off.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:23.870
Toriko-san, don't tell me this smell is...

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:28.740
Yep. I'm told there's a Durian 
Bomb Tree 100 km. ahead of us.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:31.380
100 km. ahead and it smells like this?!

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:35.550
This is my first experience 
smelling anything like this!

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:38.790
It's a first-smell... A 
first-smell explosion!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.920
What are you talking about, first-smell?!

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.660
Listen, this isn't the 
smell of the Durian Bomb.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:48.190
When the fruit gets ripe, 
it falls to the ground,

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:51.230
and releases an incredibly strong odor.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.500
I hear all vegetation in a 100 
km. radius withers in an instant

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:58.800
and fish in neighboring waters 
float to the surface...

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.410
There are all kinds of rumors.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:05.110
I can't take a murderous scent like that!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.010
Listen...

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:09.580
With a Durian Bomb, the riper it is,

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:11.780
the more delicious nutrients 
it's got stored up.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.550
In other words, the more it 
reeks, the better it tastes!

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.720
But the more delicious it is, 
the worse it smells, right?

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.030
It does stink, doesn't it, Komatsu?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.260
It stinks to high heaven!

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.860
But are you okay?

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:29.270
Your sense of smell is 10,000 times 
better than an average person's, right?

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:32.870
Yeah, but even so, I'm hangin' in 
there, so you hang in there, too!

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:37.840
Sorry! I just farted.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.810
I couldn't tell at all! Let's just go home!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.850
Like we can just go home?

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:48.320
I never turn my back on an ingredient.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.320
No matter what kind of ingredient it is...

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:55.630
If you're a pro chef, you 
can understand that, right?

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:57.730
Toriko-san...

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.130
Come on, let's go, Komatsu!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.730
Right, Toriko-san!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.470
Don't make a disgusted face!

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:06.870
Stinks...

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:10.110
What's wrong, Komatsu? Stinks...

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:14.310
Um, maybe we should've, stinks...

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:16.880
...brought along protective 
clothing to wear...

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.280
It wouldn't work! Stinks... 
It wouldn't work, Komatsu!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.720
Stinks... The Durian Bomb is a 
special preparation ingredient.

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:25.120
I know! Stinks...

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.720
I heard someone once approached one wearing 
clothing like an astronaut's suit,

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:31.560
and the fruit melted it!

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:36.730
Stinks... It's possible that only unarmed 
organisms can capture the fruit.

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:41.900
Stinks... Maybe the Durian Bomb is 
looking for someone who'll accept it

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.610
in all its reeking glory.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:44.440
Stinks...

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:48.010
D-Do you think it'll accept 
us if we make these faces?

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.450
We can't help having deformed faces...

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.950
The heart is more important!

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.420
Hold on tight to the feeling 
of "I wanna eat it!"

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:58.850
H-How about stoppin' for a lunch 
break? Even though it stinks here...

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:02.960
N-No thanks. I don't think I could eat 
anything with this stench... Stinks...

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.260
What are you talkin' about?!

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:08.030
You gotta get somethin' in your stomach 
or when we do capture it, your body...

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:14.170
What?! The smell's so bad, 
the ingredients crumbled?!

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.270
A-Are we almost there, Toriko-san?

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.710
The smell is... in my eyes!

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:22.040
My eyes! My eyes sting! Stinks!

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.410
The stink has become aggressively bad...

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:28.450
We've almost reached the Durian 
Bomb. Hang in there, Komatsu!

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:29.880
Stinks...

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:31.150
Stinks!

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:32.450
Stinks!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.220
It smells! The smell is really powerful here!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.190
We're close, Komatsu! Suck it up!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:41.430
I can't! I can't hold out any more!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.760
Komatsu, look!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.370
There it is!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.400
The Durian Bomb!

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.240
I-It's huge!

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.810
S-Stinks! Stinks!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.440
Yeah!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.510
Stinks...

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:00.880
The fruit!

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:03.750
Toriko-san, our clothes are melting!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.690
The fruit's ripe! Looks like it's gonna fall!

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:09.190
Uh-oh! Oh, boy!

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:14.660
I-It'll be okay, Komatsu!

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:15.760
It's just an odor!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:20.970
It's not like our lives are in 
danger, at least I don't think...

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.240
Those words and your face aren't 
convincing in the least.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:42.720
Stinks!

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.530
Sorry, Toriko...

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.030
D-Disgusting odor!

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:15.050
The powerful smell knocked us out?

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:16.090
Stinks!

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.560
I-I could see the River Styx...

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:20.390
Stinks!

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:26.660
This stench!　I wake up and succumb 
to it all over again... Stinks!

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.600
It's an endless loop! 
Collapse, wake up... Stinks!

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:30.070
Stinks!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:30.830
Stinks!

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:31.940
Stinks!

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.670
I haven't been back to the 
restaurant in a long time!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.080
Who would've guessed that 
it'd take us a month

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.440
to conquer the smell of and 
capture the Durian Bomb?

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.910
Let's celebrate the capture!

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.280
I'll make a lot of delicious food!

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.480
Stinks!

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:53.120
M-Maybe the smell is stuck on us?!

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:57.490
Matsu! I thought I'd have dinner 
in your restaurant for once...

00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:59.160
Disgusting odor!

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.900
Sunny-san!

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:05.700
Are we doomed to live as 
totally smelly characters?

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:13.740
Under our feet, over our heads

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:22.020
The world is spinning

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:27.190
A dream flower

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:30.860
Is blooming, blooming

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:37.970
Tell me the rest, come on

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:41.600
Lead me by the hand

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.940
And take me with you

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:52.580
Don't leave me here alone

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:56.450
Red shoes

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:59.690
I can't take off

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:10.600
I'm the only one dancing

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.970
Find Yun! Run, Run, Yun!

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:19.170
Okay, we're starting a new segment today!

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.440
Yun is hiding somewhere in the image 
you're about to see, so please find him!

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:26.750
Since this is our first time, 
Yun's hiding level is...

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:28.950
Hiding Level 1.

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.050
Can you find Yun in the allotted 
time limit of ten seconds?!

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:34.990
Let's have a heaping helping of start!

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:37.590
Have you found him yet?

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:39.690
It's too easy, you say?

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:42.690
I'll just give a one-gram hint for those 
of you who don't know where he is.

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:45.700
Something looks kind of suspicious in 
the top right part of the screen...

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:49.970
Well, did you get it?

00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:51.370
Yun is right here!

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:57.440
If you couldn't find even a gram of him,

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.510
be sure to find a heaping helping 
of him next time, okay?!

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:04.980
And following this new segment is the 
segment you've all been waiting for...

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:10.290
The bell for the greatest conflict of the century is about to ring.

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:14.120
Are we going to see the Monchy Hyper Backdrop?

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:17.430
Too Huge! The Giant Fortune Roll, 
Completed with a Pro Wrestling Move!

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:19.520
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
